course: dictionary
lesson: 1560
title: Chanting: words said again and again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chanting means saying or singing the same words over and over, often in rhythm. In «Chanting lists can help you remember, as Grandma did», the clues are lists and remember, so chanting must be a way of learning by repeating.
explain: Context shows which meaning fits. «The haka is a Māori ceremonial dance with chanting, stamping and fierce faces» tells you chanting is part of a special ceremony. Ask yourself: what would the people be doing with their voices here?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "saying the same words over and over" in place of chanting in «The crowd was chanting». If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Chanting means singing or saying words over and over, often on one or a few notes.
fact: Monks in church life sing Gregorian chant, and people in Buddhism and Hinduism chant mantras such as «Om».
fact: «The haka» is a Māori ceremonial dance with chanting, stamping and fierce faces, used for welcomes, celebrations, funerals and challenges.
fact: Fans chant the team's name at sports matches, and pupils may chant times tables to help them remember.
fact: Chant is the verb: chant, chants, chanted, chanting.
exercise: «The crowd was chanting» at the match. What does chanting mean? | Whispering a secret to a friend | *Saying or singing the same words over and over | Running very fast
exercise: «The haka is a Māori ceremonial dance with chanting, stamping and fierce faces.» Which is a use of the haka? | Only before battles | Cooking dinner for the family | *Welcomes and celebrations
exercise: Pupils may chant times tables in class. Why do they chant them? | To make a crowd angry | To win a football match | *To say the words together in rhythm so they remember them
test: «Chanting or cheering at a fight encourages it.» What does encourages mean? | Stops it at once | Makes it funnier | Makes it quieter | *Makes it more likely to happen
test: Which phrase best describes Gregorian chant? | *Monks singing the same words over and over on a few notes | Fans shouting at a goal | Dancers jumping and stamping | Children drawing pictures
exam: «Chanting lists can help you remember.» What does this tell you about chanting? | It is only done in church | It is always loud and angry | It means reading silently | *It can help you learn things by repeating them
